WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:03.290
A trader prices her strawberries too high.

2
00:00:03.290 --> 00:00:06.590
At closing time, boxes
are still stacked up.

3
00:00:06.590 --> 00:00:10.160
Next door, a baker
prices his bread too low.

4
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.590
It sells out by nine,

5
00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:13.720
and a queue is still waiting.

6
00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.040
Economists have names for these.

7
00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:18.360
Unsold stock is a surplus.

8
00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:20.840
A queue signals a shortage.

9
00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.980
So when a price is too high or too low,

10
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:27.260
what pulls it back to where
buyers and sellers agree?

11
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:30.770
In this mission, you'll find the
price where the market clears,

12
00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:32.870
and measure the gap when it doesn't.

13
00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:35.090
Then you'll set the
price yourself in a graph

14
00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:38.000
lab and see what happens to that gap.

15
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:41.120
Your mission: find out
what pulls a price back

16
00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:43.080
to where buyers and sellers agree.
